address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO TSUYOSI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIKUROHANE TOHRU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO YOSHINOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BABA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAJIMA, SOHKICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO, TSUYOSI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>Uchikurohane, Tohru</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of the utilization of a bactericidal composition characterized by treating seeds of a subject plant or a cultivation carrier for sowing the subject plant with an effective amount of a composition containing, as the active ingredient, one or more member selected from among 1,2,3-thiadiazole derivatives represented by general formula (I) and salts thereof: wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents H, (C1-6)alkyl or C3-7 cycloalkyl; and R&lt;2&gt; represents CO-Y-R&lt;3&gt; (wherein R&lt;3&gt; represents H, (halo)(C1-20)alkyl, (halo)(C2-20)alkenyl, (substituted) carbamoyl (C1-6)alkyl, (substituted) phenyl, (substituted) phenyl (C1-6)alkyl, a 5- to 6-membered heterocycle having one or more hetero atoms selected from among O, S and N, etc.). This method is superior in the effect of controlling disease injury such as Pyricularia orizae to the foliage application treatment.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un procédé d'utilisation d'une composition bactéricide caractérisé par le traitement des graines d'une plante sujet ou d'un support de culture pour semer la plante sujet avec une dose efficace d'une composition renfermant, comme ingrédient actif, un ou plusieurs éléments sélectionnés parmi des dérivés de 1,2,3-thiadiazole représentés par la formule (I) et des sels de ceux-ci, formule dans laquelle R&lt;1 &gt;représente H, (C1-6)alkyle ou C3-7 cycloalkyle; et R&lt;2&gt; représente CO-Y-R&lt;3&gt; (où R&lt;3&gt; représente H, (halo) (C1-20)alkyle, (halo) (C2-20)alcényle, carbamoyle (C1-6) alkyle (substitué), phényle (substitué), phényle (C1-6) alkyle (substitué), un hétérocycle comportant entre 5 et 6 éléments présentant un ou plusieurs hétéroatomes sélectionnés entre O, S et N, etc.). En outre, ce procédé présente des qualités supérieures en terme de suppression des lésions pathologiques provoquées par exemple par Pyricularia orizae sur le feuillage, par l'application de ce traitement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>